   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Dear TMB developers.<br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">I would like to report our findings, which might help to improve TMB.  While we have run an inference in TMB (i.e., the set of MakeADFun and nlmin) using simulated data, we found that, despite the </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">warning message, </font><span style=\"font-size:large\">“Hessian of fixed effects was not positive definite”, other output elements misled us by showing successful convergence (e.g., $convergence of 0), the presence of the covariance matrix </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:large\">of estimates (e.g.,</span><span style=\"font-size:large\"> from sdreport(model)$cov, or sdreport(model)$cov.fixed), and the presence of the standard errors of estimates, etc.  I am saying the contradiction between the warning message vs. those </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:large\">output elements that imply </span><font size=\"4\">successful </font><span style=\"font-size:large\">inferences. </span><span style=\"font-size:large\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:large\">Estimates of *the standard errors* of parameters (fixed effects) in this case were very unreasonable (yes, it makes sense thanks to the warning message),</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:large\">when being compared with the (known) true values </span><span style=\"font-size:large\">of </span><span style=\"font-size:large\">parameters </span><span style=\"font-size:large\">(fixed effects), from which data had been simulated.  </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"> </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Please see the example of our findings below.   </font></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">(1)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">   </span>Note the warning <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">message belo<font color=\"#000000\">w in red.</font></span></font></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">&gt; sdreport(xxx$model);</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">sdreport(.) result</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">               Estimate      Std. Error</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">loga       0.5260281   0.4325290</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">logb       0.4163987 218.1806116</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">logsig_p  -2.1019463   0.3286204</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">logK      17.2359107 218.1826011</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">logq     -19.4894820   3.7650666</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\">logr     -14.0591460 <a href=\"tel:(274)%20747-4254\" value=\"+12747474254\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">274.7474254</a></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif;color:red\"><font size=\"4\">Warning:</font></span></b></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif;color:red\"><font size=\"4\">    </font></span></b></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif;color:red\"><font size=\"4\">          Hessian of fixed effects was not positive definite.</font></span></b></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria Math&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Maximum gradient component: 4.912905e-05</font></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> </p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt 36pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">(2)<span style=\"font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">   </span>But the covariance matrix of estimates was generated</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;\">      &gt; sdreport(xxx$model)$cov.fixed;</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">                   loga          logb    logsig_p          logK       logq          logr</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">       loga      0.18708133 -1.569927e-02 -0.13404870 -2.011561e-01  0.2060882 -5.704039e-02</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">       logb     -0.01569927  4.760278e+04  0.01386906 -4.759614e+04 -6.5953252 -7.548696e+04</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">       logsig_p -0.13404870  1.386906e-02  0.10799136  1.642217e-01 -0.1704407  4.821895e-02</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">       logK     -0.20115615 -4.759614e+04  0.16422169  4.760365e+04 -7.5518510  7.547677e+04</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">       logq      0.20608823 -6.595325e+00 -0.17044069 -7.551851e+00 14.1757265  1.014200e+01</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">       logr     -0.05704039 -7.548696e+04  0.04821895  7.547677e+04 10.1420020  7.548615e+04</span><span style=\"font-size:8pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\"></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt 36pt;line-height:17.12px;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Suggestion:   If you think our findings are valid, then it may be a good idea to follow the custom of ADMB.  For instance, if Hessian matrix is not positive definite, COR file is not generated under ADMB.  </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">A user *immediately* gets a sense by finding the absence of COR file that the corresponding numerical optimization is not reliable .  On the other hand, a user would be tricked under TMB unless he/she</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">carefully searches the warning message.   Especially when a user runs an inference in TMB, using thousands of sets of simulated data, he/she would have to manually find the warning message per run; nobody</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">would want to do so thousand times.   If Hessian matrix is not positive definite, your setting the convergence flag to be 1 (Failure) not 0 (Success), or your replacing the covariance matrix of</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">estimates by NA under TMB would be consistent, more importantly helping a user to quickly discard such unreliable inferences.</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Thank you very much for your great development of TMB, and also thank you in advance for your reading this email.</font></p><font color=\"#888888\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Saang-Yoon Hyun, and Kyuhan Kim</font></p></font></div>\r\n"
