   "subject": "Re: Contradictory messages",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi.</div>Now I find that \r\n\r\n&quot;sdreport( ... $model)$pdHess&quot; indicates whether the uncertainty of estimates is reliable or not.   When there is the warning message (&quot;Warning: Hessian of fixed effects was not positive definite&quot;), &quot;sdreport( ... $model)$pdHess&quot; returns FALSE, and, as expected, estimates of the standard errors of some parameter estimates were extremely unreasonable.  Again, under such cases, it might be a good idea to discard uncertainty values (e.g., SE, covariance matrix, etc.) or to replace them by NA.   Thank you,<div>Saang-Yoon<br><div>  </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Wed, Mar 18, 2020 at 2:05 PM Saang-Yoon Hyun &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shy...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Dear TMB developers.<br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">I would like to report our findings, which might help to improve TMB.  While we have run an inference in TMB (i.e., the set of MakeADFun and nlmin) using simulated data, we found that, despite the </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">warning message, </font><span style=\"font-size:large\">“Hessian of fixed effects was not positive definite”, other output elements misled us by showing successful convergence (e.g., $convergence of 0), the presence of the covariance matrix </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:large\">of estimates (e.g.,</span><span style=\"font-size:large\"> from sdreport(model)$cov, or sdreport(model)$cov.fixed), and the presence of the standard errors of estimates, etc.  I am saying the contradiction between the warning message vs. those </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:large\">output elements that imply </span><font si