e-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Suggestion:   If you think our findings are valid, then it may be a good idea to follow the custom of ADMB.  For instance, if Hessian matrix is not positive definite, COR file is not generated under ADMB.  </font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">A user *immediately* gets a sense by finding the absence of COR file that the corresponding numerical optimization is not reliable .  On the other hand, a user would be tricked under TMB unless he/she</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">carefully searches the warning message.   Especially when a user runs an inference in TMB, using thousands of sets of simulated data, he/she would have to manually find the warning message per run; nobody</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">would want to do so thousand times.   If Hessian matrix is not positive definite, your setting the convergence flag to be 1 (Failure) not 0 (Success), or your replacing the covariance matrix of</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">estimates by NA under TMB would be consistent, more importantly helping a user to quickly discard such unreliable inferences.</font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Thank you very much for your great development of TMB, and also thank you in advance for your reading this email.</font></p><font color=\"#888888\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:13.91px;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><font size=\"4\">Saang-Yoon Hyun, and Kyuhan Kim</font></p></font></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
